hanged controls run by this evaluator (fresh dependencies)\\n\\n- `node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run tests/diagnostics/windows-p1-stages.test.ts\\n  --reporter=json --outputFile=<owned report path>`: exit 0, **81/81 passed**, 0 failed, 0 pending.\\n  All 14 `required_future_controls` describe blocks present and passing. Raw JSON/stdout/stderr in\\n  `raw/unchanged81.*`. The unchanged `checksSummary` validator accepts this raw report\\n  (`allRequiredControlsPassed: true`, `releaseAcceptance: false`) — exercised inside my own suite.\\n- `npm run verify` (`prisma generate && tsc --noEmit`): exit 0, both before and after adding the\\n  new evaluator test file (raw logs `raw/npmrunverify*.stdout/stderr.txt`).\\n\\n## Own additive checks (tests/evaluator/windows-p1-checkout-r1-20261011.test.ts, 59/59 pass)\\n\\nCompact table-driven, derived independently (no reuse of the previous evaluator's tests/outputs):\\n\\n1. HEAD/parent identity; five file hashes; exact 8-path diff closure; filtered tree-inventory\\n   equality; ten prior/frozen hashes vs disk bytes; scoped clean status.\\n2. Exact byte projections above, re-derived in-test from source888 via `git show`.\\n3. Checkout-env exact-byte confinement oracle (byte identity vs the declared candidate hash —\\n   **not** a YAML parser): positive on the real workflow; 30 negatives across missing env,\\n   count `'0'`/`'2'`, second pair, duplicate/extra key, non-string scalars, false value,\\n   workflow/job/later-step (setup-node, prepare, npm ci, synthetic, INITIAL, seal, verify,\\n   upload) leakage, `GITHUB_ENV` write, global/system config writes, sparse/path changes,\\n   new command probe, secret reference, permissions broadening, continue-on-error, event/ref\\n   change, upload-path alteration — each verified to differ and to fail the oracle. Line-level\\n   structural positives confirm the env block sits only in the checkout step.\\n4. Binding identity: CLI literals equal on-disk JSON/MD SHA-256 (positive proven